fb: allow the PM8150L WLED reads on raphael (SID 5, not PMI8998 SID 3)

raphael's backlight WLED is in the PM8150L at SPMI usid 5 (reg <0xd800>,
<0xd900>, interrupts <0x5 0xd8 ...>), not PMI8998 usid 3. The SPMI read
whitelist for the non-beryllium branch only accepts sid 0, so blInit could
not read the WLED brightness, fBlOK stayed false and the backlight never
followed iOS. Extend the else branch to also accept sid 5 for the WLED
control/sink peripherals (0xd8/0xd9).

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c
@@ -131,3 +131,4 @@ sweet_spmi_read(unsigned sid, unsigned addr, uint8_t *out)
 	} else {
-		allowed = sid == 0 && (peripheral == 0x10 || peripheral == 0x11 ||
-		    peripheral == 0x12 || peripheral == 0x13 || peripheral == 0x48);
+		allowed = (sid == 0 && (peripheral == 0x10 || peripheral == 0x11 ||
+		    peripheral == 0x12 || peripheral == 0x13 || peripheral == 0x48)) ||
+		    (sid == 5 && (peripheral == 0xd8 || peripheral == 0xd9));
